{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Floorp-Projects/Floorp-Runtime/pulls/84","id":4797714944,"node_id":"PR_kwDONoernc8AAAABHfdSAA","html_url":"https://github.com/Floorp-Projects/Floorp-Runtime/pull/84","diff_url":"https://github.com/Floorp-Projects/Floorp-Runtime/pull/84.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Floorp-Projects/Floorp-Runtime/pull/84.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Floorp-Projects/Floorp-Runtime/issues/84","number":84,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add limited Debug source and native bundle proof contracts","user":{"login":"Ryosuke-Asano","id":73892113,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODkyMTEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73892113?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryosuke-Asano","html_url":"https://github.com/Ryosuke-Asano","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryosuke-Asano/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryosuke-Asano/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryosuke-Asano/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryosuke-Asano/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryosuke-Asano/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryosuke-Asano/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryosuke-Asano/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryosuke-Asano/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ryosuke-Asano/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The shadow QA3 contracts did not ingest a complete Runtime checkout or connect a same-build Mozilla test-support bundle to a separate cold consumer. This change adds that producer/consumer recipe for a limited Linux x64 Debug proof: exact U/R/P/C/B/D/F source transitions, effective tests/debug configure checks, separate primary/support artifacts, and fixed browser-chrome/xpcshell cases plus assertion canaries. The mozlog consumer also rejects missing, boolean or floating-point child exit codes that previously compared equal to zero.\n\nThis is a stacked Draft PR with base `codex/qa3-shadow-foundation`. Dependencies: [Runtime #83](https://github.com/Floorp-Projects/Floorp-Runtime/pull/83) and [Floorp #2889](https://github.com/Floorp-Projects/Floorp/pull/2889). [The proof interface](https://github.com/Floorp-Projects/Floorp-Runtime/blob/460106115bc76b026c8bf8dad24df7fcb07f97c2/.github/qa/linux-debug-proof.md) describes the private caller, pinned launcher/toolchain/offline-dependency interface and launch prerequisites.\n\nThe private reusable workflow authenticates workflow/recipe/run/attempt and artifact identities, keeps controller credentials outside native execution, and rejects missing, skipped, retried, mutated or incomplete evidence. Archive expansion, retained logs, disk reserves, cgroup limits and owned descendant cleanup are bounded. The xpcshell adapter explicitly disables Mozilla's automation retry through its API while preserving normal exit semantics. Existing public build, QA, PGO and publication workflows are unchanged. The final typed-exit follow-up changes only `qa3_mozlog.py` and one regression method, covering eight invalid values and valid integer zero.\n\nValidation: all local Runtime unit contracts **162 PASS** (69 existing + 93 QA3); Ruff check/format, targeted `mach lint --linter ruff` and `git diff --check` pass. Two independent reviewers confirmed the typed-exit fix and its initial three failing subtests. The user-provided kit at Floorp commit `87311566a225936fbe7948db142bce3f1d3379d8` was reviewed separately: original **114 PASS**, repaired **130 PASS**. Its three P1 repairs, immutable original ZIP, separate repair archive, readable patch and raw initial failures are submitted in [Floorp #2893](https://github.com/Floorp-Projects/Floorp/pull/2893); the kit is not installed into active Floorp tools or substituted for these Runtime contracts. Related Floorp host checks remain **16 + 106 PASS**. Initial development and outer-test-envelope failures are retained separately with their diagnostics.\n\nAutomatic lightweight PR CI: [run 37933305289, attempt 1](https://github.com/Floorp-Projects/Floorp-Runtime/actions/runs/37933305289) at commit `460106115bc76b026c8bf8dad24df7fcb07f97c2`. REST reports success for the contracts job and every step, including preflight and evidence upload. This records CI metadata; raw CI stdout/test counts are unverified. Local 162 tests are independently recorded.\n\nFull `mach lint` remains blocked by the sparse review checkout's missing `third_party/node/pnpm-lock.yaml`. No private Runtime Debug build/harness workflow was dispatched. Private workers, UID/cgroup/launcher enforcement and cold offline dependencies remain unprovisioned and unmeasured. Authenticated source-cohort, cross-run first-failure history and final signed artifact qualification remain incomplete.\n\n**Launch remains No-Go.** `nativeQualification` and `productArtifactQualification` remain `UNVERIFIED`, and `publicationAuthorized=false`, even after a future limited consumer PASS. This PR does not qualify signed production artifacts, other OS/architectures or publication. No Blacksmith provisioning/paid run, infrastructure or credential changes, native dispatch, merge, signing, notarization or release was performed.\n\nThe companion Floorp docs PR automatically triggered its existing prebuilt Runtime/browser integration workflow. That owned run was cancelled after the Linux browser step had started; its partial results are not qualification. The local synthetic validation above is separate from that automatic CI event.\n","created_at":"2026-10-09T07:57:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T13:11:21Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1259c3dca14ba971edd20ccd9317fbc027c2c2a5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Floorp-Proje